# Global git ignore (linked to ~/.config/git/ignore, which git reads by
# default in every repo): a safety net so a loose API key or env file is
# not swept up by `git add -A` in any project. Ignoring is not blocking:
# a file can still be force-added on purpose, so real keys belong in
# ~/.config/secrets/, outside every repo.
.env
.env.*
secrets/
*.key
